@@ -5,11 +5,59 @@ This repository is designed to remotely control StackChan servo movements via th
 ## Applicable Devices
 
 * StickC-Plus + Hat Mini JoyC
+* StickS3 + Unit Joystick2
 
 ## Compilation Environment
 
-* IDF：ESP-IDF v5.4.2
-* Device Type：esp32
+* ESP-IDF v5.4.2
+* StickC-Plus target: `esp32`
+* StickS3 target: `esp32s3`
+
+## StickS3 + Unit Joystick2 Notes
+
+This firmware now defaults to StickS3 PORT.A + Unit Joystick2:
+
+* Unit Joystick2 I2C address: `0x63`
+* StickS3 PORT.A SDA/SCL: GPIO9/GPIO10
+* Joystick raw range: `0..65535`, center `32768`
+* StickS3 build uses an 8MB flash configuration and `partitions_sticks3.csv`
+* ESP-NOW packet format is unchanged: `[target-id][yaw int16][pitch int16][speed int16][laser uint8]`
+
+Before building for StickS3, switch the ESP-IDF target:
+
+```bash
+idf.py set-target esp32s3
+idf.py build
+idf.py flash
+```
+
+To create a single `0x0` image for M5Burner, run this from an ESP-IDF PowerShell/Command Prompt:
+
+```powershell
+.\package_sticks3_m5burner.ps1
+```
+
+The output is `StackChan-RemoteControl-StickS3-Joystick2_0x0.bin`.
+
+If you are using the ESP-IDF Command Prompt (`cmd.exe`), use:
+
+```cmd
+package_sticks3_m5burner.cmd
+```
+
+On the StackChan firmware side, open the `ESPNOW.REMOTE` app, choose `Receiver`, and use the same Wi-Fi channel and receiver ID as the remote.
+
+## Controls
+
+* BtnA click: switch Setup / Running / IMU screens
+* BtnA hold on Running screen: open joystick settings
+* BtnA click on joystick settings: return to Running screen
+* BtnB on Setup screen: select Channel or Receiver ID
+* BtnB on Running/IMU screen: toggle laser flag
+* BtnB on joystick settings: select Invert X or Invert Y
+* Joystick up/down on joystick settings: toggle the selected inversion option
+
+Joystick inversion settings are saved to NVS and restored after reboot.
 
